🏗️ High-Level Architecture
Before we dive into the code, here is how these pieces will play together:

Express Backend: Acts as your API gateway, handling authentication and routing.

OpenAI SDK: The "brains" inside your Express routes, processing prompts and returning AI magic.

Docker: To package your Express app into a portable container.

Kubernetes: To manage those containers, ensuring "My Tacklebox" stays afloat even if traffic spikes.

my-tacklebox/
├── node_modules/         # Created by npm install
├── src/                  # All your application logic
│   └── server.js         # The Express code we wrote
├── k8s/                  # Kubernetes manifest files
│   ├── deployment.yaml   # Defines your pods and replicas
│   ├── service.yaml      # Defines how to access the app
│   └── secrets.yaml      # Your encrypted OpenAI API keys
├── .env                  # LOCAL ONLY: Secrets for dev (ignore in git)
├── .gitignore            # Tells Git to ignore .env and node_modules
├── .dockerignore         # Tells Docker to ignore node_modules
├── Dockerfile            # Instructions to build the image
└── package.json          # App dependencies and scripts